    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, we're having some issues on the production line here. our sublimation heat press isn't transferring the ink properly onto the polyester blends. the colors look washed out and patchy even when we follow the standard settings. can you help me troubleshoot the temperature and pressure requirements?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Washed-out and patchy sublimation transfer on polyester blends usually means the heat or pressure isn't quite right for the ink to properly bond with the fabric. Try increasing your temperature by 10-20 degrees Fahrenheit, and simultaneously, check your pressure gauge to ensure you are applying consistent, firm pressure across the entire surface. If the issue persists, you might need to increase the press time slightly, as some polyester blends require a longer \"soak\" time for the ink to fully migrate. Remember, the correct heat and pressure are crucial for a vibrant, solid color transfer.",
      "source": "target",
