    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "we tried bumping the temp and increasing the pressure like you said, but it didn't really help much. the patches are still there, almost like parts of the design are just disappearing or not picking up at all in specific spots. we checked the ink sublimated paper and it seems fine. is there anything else that could cause the ink to not \"take\" to the fabric properly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If increasing the heat and pressure didn't solve the patchy issue, it's likely related to the preparation or the materials themselves. First, ensure your polyester blends are *actual* polyester, not a blend with too much cotton content, as cotton is a major inhibitor to sublimation. A good quality, high-grade polyester is essential for the ink to bond properly. Also, check the surface of the fabric for any oils, sizing, or pre-treatments, as these residues can repel the ink, making it look like it's disappearing.",
      "source": "target",
